---
// src/pages/about.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HonestyBadge from '../components/HonestyBadge.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site.js';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Why I Built This"
  description="The honest story behind Chitra Sampada: why I built this watch companion, the two problems it solves, and how community suggestions work."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-20 space-y-16">
    
    <!-- Header / Intro -->
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-slate-400">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-red-400 font-medium">About</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white tracking-tight leading-tight">
        Why I built this site.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        A personal note on what this project is, the headaches that led me to make it, and how it works.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Main Essay / Story Content -->
    <div class="space-y-12 text-slate-300 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed font-normal">
      
      <!-- Section: The Beginner Headache -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">
          Nobody tells you this stuff when you start watching.
        </h2>
        <p>
          I'm an anime, movie, and web series lover myself. But when I first got into anime, I ran into things that nobody ever explains to a beginner up front.
        </p>
        <p>
          For example: I had no idea what "filler" even meant. I'd sit through dozens of episodes where the plot suddenly came to a complete halt, wondering what happened, only to find out months later that it was non-canon filler that never existed in the original story.
        </p>
        <p>
          Then there was the watch order problem. You find a series you want to try, only to discover it has three seasons, two movies, a prequel OVA, and a spin-off. Looking up what order to watch them in is a minefield of spoilers on forums and confusing wiki pages. It shouldn't take research just to figure out what episode to click on first.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: What to watch next -->
      <section class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-white/10">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">
          The post-show exhaustion.
        </h2>
        <p>
          The second big problem happened every time I finished a show I loved. You finish the last episode, feel that void, and sit down to find what to watch next.
        </p>
        <p>
          An hour passes, and you're still scrolling through endless lists on massive databases. Every title has hundreds of mixed reviews, fan debates, and 10/10 scores from people who loved everything. You end up with decision fatigue and watch nothing.
        </p>
        <p>
          That's really why I built this. Not to list every single title in existence — there are already plenty of massive databases out there that do that, and they do it well. This solves a much narrower, practical problem: giving you a clean, honest list with the context you actually need before you start.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: How this site works -->
      <section class="space-y-6 pt-4 border-t border-white/10">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">
          How this site works: Watched vs. Watchlist
        </h2>
        <p>
          Instead of listing thousands of shows I've never touched, this site only has two categories of titles:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-2">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-[#0b0f19] border border-white/10 space-y-2.5">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <HonestyBadge status="watched" size="sm" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white">Personally Watched</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
              Titles I have actually sat down and finished from start to end. If it's labeled "Watched", you know the recommendation comes from first-hand viewing, with exact filler notes and watch order.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-[#0b0f19] border border-white/10 space-y-2.5">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <HonestyBadge status="watchlist" size="sm" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white">On My Watchlist</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
              Titles I haven't watched yet, but plan to watch next. I include them so you can see what's on deck and follow along, but I clearly label them so I never pretend I've finished something I haven't.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-400">
          That clarity is the whole point. Anyone visiting can make their own choice with real context, without guessing whether the person writing about it ever actually watched it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: Community Suggestions -->
      <section id="suggestions" class="space-y-6 pt-6 border-t border-white/10">
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-red-400">
            Real Input
          </span>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">
            Suggestions from real people
          </h2>
        </div>

        <p>
          I also want this to grow with input from people who love good stories. If you think an anime, movie, or series is missing, or if you have a better watch order recommendation, I genuinely want to hear it.
        </p>

        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-red-950/30 via-[#0d1220] to-[#0b0f19] border border-white/10 space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-400" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
            </svg>
            <span>My Honest Pledge on Suggestions</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            If someone sends in a suggestion and it gets added to the site, <strong>it will always be clearly marked as a user suggestion with your name or username</strong>. It will never be silently blended in as if it was my personal pick. Real attribution matters.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Suggestion contact form / mailto box -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/10 space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white">
            Have a suggestion or correction?
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400">
            Send an email with the title, whether you've watched it, and any watch-order notes or filler tips you think others would find helpful.
          </p>
          <div class="pt-2 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center gap-3">
            <a
              href="mailto:suggestions@chitrasampada.com?subject=Anime%20Suggestion%20for%20Chitra%20Sampada"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-red-600 hover:bg-red-500 text-white font-semibold text-xs transition-colors"
            >
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 8l7.89 5.26a2 2 0 002.22 0L21 8M5 19h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z" />
              </svg>
              <span>Send a Suggestion via Email</span>
            </a>
            <span class="text-xs text-slate-400">
              (Or connect via our upcoming community channels)
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>

      </section>

      <!-- Bottom Navigation -->
      <div class="pt-10 border-t border-white/10 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
          Ready to see what's on the list?
        </p>
        <a
          href="/anime"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/15 text-white text-sm font-semibold border border-white/10 transition-colors"
        >
          <span>Explore the Anime Catalog</span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
